# A probabilistic choice whose weight 3/2 is not a probability: the program has no meaning.
# Expected: refused with one line naming the weight.  The rule 3/2 * wp(S1, f) - 1/2 * wp(S2, f)
# used to be applied as it stands, giving the expectation of c as -1, so the bound below was
# proved for a program none of whose runs ends with c below 0.
nat c;
{
	c := 0;
}[3/2]{
	c := 2;
}
?Ex [c] <= 0
